// Local signing settings, read by project.yml's target-level configFiles
// and applied via xcodegen's generated baseConfigurationReference — see
// the "Signing / building a release archive" section of README.md.
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is your 10-character Apple Developer Team ID (Apple
// Developer > Membership, or the account menu in Xcode > Settings >
// Accounts). It is not a secret — visible in App Store Connect URLs and
// exported archive metadata — but it's account-specific, so it stays out
// of project.yml itself and lives here instead where it won't collide
// with anyone else building this project under their own team.
//
// Fill in your own Team ID below. Leaving it blank is fine for opening
// and editing the project — Xcode will prompt for a team the first time
// it actually needs to sign something (running on a device, archiving).
//
// Edit this file directly rather than picking a team in Xcode's Signing
// & Capabilities tab — xcodegen owns project.pbxproj (see README.md) and
// a future `xcodegen generate` would discard a value Xcode wrote there
// instead of here.
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = Y9HYKHB3X9
